TITLE:: REScoreRecorder
summary:: Records what you do to a song into an REScore
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScore, Classes/RETap, Classes/RCSong

DESCRIPTION::
One per song, through link::Classes/RCSong#-scoreRecorder::. Off (not armed): nothing installed, nothing checked beyond code::RETap.active::. Armed: the taps reach it, nothing is kept. Recording: events are appended; the file is written at code::stop::. The recorder only observes: no random draw, no scheduling beyond the quantized start (one Function on the song's clock), no server message. See the reCording guide, "Scores".

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: song
argument:: root
The folder of the take files, nil to keep the score in code::lastScore:: only.
argument:: version
The wersion in the file name.
argument:: piece

METHOD:: allInputs
code::[\midi, \osc, \keyboard, \actions, \code]::.

METHOD:: unsafeCode
A code line containing one of these strings is kept but marked code::replay: false::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: arm
argument:: scope
nil (the whole song), or objects (layers, beats, batches, orgnsms, fobjects, crawlers, the song's code::midi::, code::osc:: or code::keyboard::) and mapping, def or device names. An event is kept when its object, or what holds it, is in the scope.
argument:: inputs
The kinds of event: every one but code::\rawMidi:: by default. code::\rawMidi:: (every MIDI message of every device, replayed by dispatching through MIDIIn) replaces code::\midi:: and code::\keyboard::.
argument:: voices
An Event: voice name → the objects and names grouped under it. nil keeps the voices added so far, an empty Event clears them.
argument:: voicesByLayer
A beat's default voice is its layer (true) or code::layer/name:: (false).

METHOD:: addVoice
argument:: name
argument:: members
Objects and names (mappings, defs, devices) grouped under the name; a member moves to the new voice.
METHOD:: removeVoice
argument:: name
METHOD:: voiceFor
argument:: objOrName
The voice it would be recorded under.
METHOD:: voicesByLayer

METHOD:: addControl
argument:: name
argument:: spec
A link::Classes/ControlSpec:: or a dictionary (min, max, warp, default, unit): written into every take's code::controls::; nil keeps the spec given before.
argument:: get
code::{ value }::: a snapshot holds the control's value.
argument:: set
code::{ |value| }::: a recall or a morph brings it back (a morph ramps it along the spec's warp).
METHOD:: controls
METHOD:: controlGetter
METHOD:: controlSetter
argument:: name
METHOD:: controlNames
The controls with a getter.

METHOD:: disarm
Stops a recording, removes the hooks.

METHOD:: record
argument:: quant
nil: now; else the take starts on that grid of the song's clock.
argument:: snapshotAtStart
Sets link::#-startSnapshot::.

METHOD:: stop
returns:: The link::Classes/REScore::, written to code::<root>/<stamp>_<song> <version>.json:: when root is set.

METHOD:: snapshot
argument:: name
The state of what is in scope: the sources of every key of the beats, the static attributes of the orgnsms, the song's seed.
returns:: The event id.

METHOD:: recall
argument:: name
Sets the state of the latest snapshot of that name (of the current take, else of the last score) at once; recorded as a morph event of 0 beats.

METHOD:: morph
argument:: name
argument:: beats
Numeric sources ramp to the snapshot's over this many beats (link::Classes/REScorePlayer#*applyState::).
returns:: The event id, nil when not recording (the state is applied all the same).

METHOD:: overdub
argument:: scorearg
The score to play and record over.
argument:: voices
The voices overdubbed (nil: all).
argument:: mode
code::\replace::, code::\keep::, code::\touch:: or nil (touch for continuous controls, replace for the rest); see link::Classes/REScore#*merge::.
argument:: punch
code::[in, out]:: in score beats (nil: from the start to the stop).
argument:: loop
Play [in, out] again and again, each pass an overdub.
argument:: quant
Both start on that grid of the song's clock (nil: now).
code::stop:: merges and writes the merge as a new file.

METHOD:: player
The link::Classes/REScorePlayer:: of the current overdub.

METHOD:: state
code::\off::, code::\armed:: or code::\recording::.
METHOD:: isArmed
METHOD:: isRecording
METHOD:: score
The score being recorded.
METHOD:: lastScore
METHOD:: beat0
METHOD:: time0
METHOD:: root
METHOD:: version
METHOD:: piece
METHOD:: startSnapshot
A take starts with a snapshot named code::start:: (true by default).
METHOD:: scope
METHOD:: inputs
METHOD:: voices

EXAMPLES::

code::
~rec = ~song.scoreRecorder(root: ~piece_dir +/+ "Scores", version: "w1");
~rec.arm(scope: [~song.layer(\core), ~batch], inputs: #[\midi, \actions], voices: (lead: [~beat1, ~beat2]));
~rec.record([4, 0]);
~rec.snapshot(\intro);
~rec.stop;
~rec.disarm;
::
